  "body": "Removes the `legal?(csr_value)` key from all CSR field definitions and the corresponding schema property. Schema version bumped to `v0.2` per versioning policy (any schema change requires a new release).\n\n## CSR YAML changes\nRemoved `legal?(csr_value)` blocks from 7 field definitions across 5 files:\n- `hstatus.yaml` – VGEIN\n- `mstatus.yaml` – MPP, SPP\n- `misa.yaml` – F, Q\n- `Smrnmi/mnstatus.yaml` – MNPP\n- `mconfigptr.yaml` – ADDRESS\n\n## Schema changes (`spec/schemas/csr_schema.json`)\n- Removed `legal?(csr_value)` from the `csr_field` object definition\n- Bumped `$id` from `v0.1` → `v0.2`\n\n## Documentation changes\n- Removed `legal?(csr_value)` table entry from `spec/std/isa/csr/schema.adoc`\n- Updated `spec/schemas/README.adoc` Schema Versions table to add a `v0.2` row for `csr_schema.json` and reflect that other schemas remain at `v0.1`\n\n## Consumer updates\n- Updated hard-coded `v0.1/csr_schema.json#` assertion in `tools/ruby-gems/udb/test/test_yaml_resolver.rb` to `v0.2/csr_schema.json#` to match the new schema version\n\nNo `.layout` files required changes (none contained `legal?`). Resolved schemas under `gen/schemas/` are gitignored and will be regenerated by the `schema-release` CI workflow on merge.\n\n<!-- START COPILOT ORIGINAL PROMPT -->\n\n\n\n<details>\n\n<summary>Original prompt</summary>\n\nThis pull request removes the `legal?` key from all YAML files under `spec/**/csr/`. Additionally, it updates the corresponding schemas in `spec/schema/` by removing the `legal?` property. \n\n### Changes:\n- Search and remove the `legal?` property in all relevant YAML files under `spec/**/csr/`.\n- Modify `.layout` files if necessary for schema regeneration using the `gen:arch` Rake task.\n- Bump the version of affected schemas by following the README guidelines on schema versioning. Specifically:\n  - Update the `$id` field for updated schemas to reflect the new version.\n  - Retain compatibility by only updating affected schema versions.\n  - Regenerate schema files using `./do gen:schema`.\n\n### Validation:\n- Ensure all modified files align with the repository’s expectations.\n- Ensure that CI checks pass post-modifications.\n\nThe following is the prior conversation context from the user's chat exploration (may be truncated):\n\nUser: Can you author and submit a PR for me?\n\nAssistant: Could you provide more details about the changes you'd like me to include in the pull request or about the purpose of the PR? For example, are there specific modifications, fixes, or features you want to add? And which branch should the PR be based on?\n\nUser: I want to remove the legal? key from any YAML file under spec/**/csr/. I also want the legal? property removed from the corresponding schemas in spec/schema. Some YAML files are generated from a .layout in the same directory. The layout should be modified, if needed. The generated files are created with the gen:arch Rake task.\n\nAssistant: Understood. Just to clarify:\n\n1. **Task Objective**:\n   - Remove the `legal?` key from YAML files under `spec/**/csr/`.\n   - Update the corresponding schemas in `spec/schema/` to remove the `legal?` property.\n   - If any YAML files are generated from a `.layout`, then the `.layout` should also be modified to reflect this removal.\n   - The `gen:arch` Rake task should still be able to regenerate files without any issues.\n\n2. **Confirmation**:\n   - Does the repository's base branch follow the default (like `main`)? Or would you like the PR to target a specific branch?\n   - Should the PR title and description summarize this change, or do you have specific text you'd like me to use?\n\nLet me know, and I'll proceed!\n\nUser: Target main branch. Generate a PR tile and body. Also bump the version of any affected schema. You can read how versioning is maintained for the schemas in a README file.\n\nAssistant: I’m unable to immediately locate detailed information on schema versioning from the repository context. Howe